    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109345" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποτελ-ίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, a name given by Herillus <i><span class="en">
			<u>Stoic.</u>
			1.91
		</span></i> to <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a subordinate
				object, which ought to be only held as a means towards attaining
				the chief good</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέλος</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				2.7.3c
			</span></i> (Madvig, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποτελές</span> codd.), <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i></div>
